From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZoeHao2026 <ZoeHao2026@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] dxgkrnl: fix syncobj reference leak in open_syncobj_from_syncfile

Sync the ported dxgkrnl delta up to Microsoft tagging point
linux-msft-wsl-6.18.40.1 (previously 6.18.35.2) and take the one
behavioural fix it carries for this code path.

dxgkio_open_syncobj_from_syncfile() only released its reference on the
error path. On success the dxgsyncobject created for the caller stayed
referenced forever, so every successful
D3DKMT_OPENSYNCOBJECTFROMSYNCFILE ioctl leaked one object plus its
shared syncpoint reference.

Restore the intended lifetime handling: on failure destroy the local
object and tell the host to drop the remote one; on success put the
reference that the ioctl took.

Scope note - the rest of the 6.18.35.2 -> 6.18.40.1 delta needs no
change on this tree:

 - drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgvmbus.h and dxgvmbus.c are already equivalent:
   0002 already converts the trailer to a flexible array member and
   fixes the corresponding cmd_size arithmetic, and Microsoft's
   current_pos spelling addresses the same bytes as &command[1].
 - include/linux/hyperv.h needs nothing: the VMBus version/channel-flag
   refactor and the paravisor flags 40.1 carries were pushed upstream
   and are already present in Linux 7.2.8.

The three driver files are byte-identical to their 40.1 counterparts
after this patch, except for the current_pos spelling above.
---
 drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgsyncfile.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgsyncfile.c b/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgsyncfile.c
--- a/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgsyncfile.c
+++ b/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgsyncfile.c
@@ -297,9 +297,14 @@
 cleanup:
 	if (dmafence)
 		dma_fence_put(dmafence);
-	if (ret) {
-		if (syncobj) 
+	if (syncobj) {
+		if (ret) {
 			dxgsyncobject_destroy(process, syncobj);
+			if (openargs.sync_object.v)
+				dxgvmb_send_destroy_sync_object(process, openargs.sync_object);
+		} else {
+			kref_put(&syncobj->syncobj_kref, dxgsyncobject_release);
+		}
 	}
 	if (adapter)
 		dxgadapter_release_lock_shared(adapter);
diff --git a/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgvmbus.c b/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgvmbus.c
diff --git a/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgvmbus.h b/drivers/hv/dxgkrnl/dxgvmbus.h
